# round B21 (w166): round 131's release rule on round 135's store: the linear MOMA store in the affine slot, the affine's parameters frozen until epoch 5 and until the trailing five-epoch validation Pearson reaches 0.15 (--ess-affine-start-epoch 5 --ess-affine-start-val-pearson 0.15), on the deletion-only graph, six seeds; paired against w154_bxdelmoma (the same store, affine from epoch 0) and w148_bxdelstorer15 (the GLPK store under the same rule). Round 131 read the rule as keeping the store's level with the best ensemble call (6.19); round 135 read the MOMA store at the parsimonious store's rank with half its spread and the best single-seed call (4.99).
